# RC1 integration contract: GNU Classpath 0.99 headless font peer
#
# This is an assembly contract, not a fabricated historical diff.
# Apply only against the exact GNU Classpath 0.99 source used by the RG35XX/JamVM build.
# Source basis and acceptance criteria: docs/RC1-FONT-HEADLESS-PEER-AUDIT.md
#
# REPLACED assumption:
#   missing org.recompile.mobile.RG35XXFontEngine owns bitmap metrics/rasterization.
#
# RC1 owner:
#   gnu.java.awt.peer.headless.HeadlessToolkit + one real ClasspathFontPeer
#   (prefer existing gnu.java.awt.font.OpenTypeFontPeer/FontDelegate path),
#   consumed by existing FreeJ2ME PlatformFont/PlatformGraphics.
#
# Required integration operations:
#
# 1. HeadlessToolkit must implement both font-peer entry paths used by java.awt.Font:
#      protected FontPeer getFontPeer(String name, int style)
#      public ClasspathFontPeer getClasspathFontPeer(String name, Map attrs)
#    They must return a non-null peer backed by a valid delegate.
#
# 2. Reuse/cache the existing OpenTypeFontPeer or another existing ClasspathFontPeer.
#    Do not instantiate/load/map a font file for every drawString call.
#
# 3. Provide a deterministic target font mapping/resource during platform assembly.
#    No guessed host font path is accepted. Resource ownership and license must be explicit.
#
# 4. If mapped font/delegate initialization fails, fail during platform/font initialization
#    with a clear diagnostic. Never keep a peer with fontDelegate == null; historical logs
#    show this later explodes in Font.hashCode/createGlyphVector/AbstractGraphics2D.drawString.
#
# 5. Do not patch java.awt.Font getters/hashCode/createGlyphVector to tolerate null peer.
#    That would mask the broken backend and produce inconsistent metrics/layout.
#
# 6. Do not globally sanitize Unicode to ASCII in PlatformGraphics.
#    Missing-glyph fallback must preserve layout/width semantics.
#
# 7. Existing FreeJ2ME PlatformFont size/face/style and PlatformGraphics anchor/clip behavior
#    remain authoritative. This patch must not create a second font facade or text renderer.
#
# Build/validation gates:
# - exact GNU Classpath tree present in reproducible source assembly;
# - authoritative font resource present;
# - non-null peer/delegate for SansSerif/Dialog/Monospaced;
# - Font.hashCode/createGlyphVector/FontMetrics smoke probes pass on JamVM;
# - target game corpus passes font rendering without safe-ASCII fallback diagnostics.
